00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.080
<b>Character Evaluation</b>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.080
<b>Enzo Bron is a French businessman and engineer. 
He also has an honorary knighthood. He is currently
the CEO of global IT business, the Shake Hands 
Corporation. Formerly, the CEO of Lyons Telecom
 and Olig Technology. The eldest child of geographer 
Alan Bron and Italian screenwriter/actress 
Renata Ricorellino, he was born in Lyons. After 
graduating from École Polytechnique, he moved 
to America to work as a researcher at Stanford,
 founding Shake Hands with the friends he made there.</b>

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.490
<b>Enzo Bron has created innovative network services that 
have caused debate worldwide. He's received criticism 
on the use of personal data from social network 
platforms to predict the actions of individuals with
 the "Futuric-Logger" service which led to him being 
subpoenaed to appear before the U.S. Senate Judiciary 
Committee.</b>

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.490
<b>There, after a tough line of questioning by Arizona 
senator, Anna Winsgate, he bit back, saying: "My
 service can prove you've been providing special 
favors to a <i>certain</i> business." This remark resulted in 
calls for Bron to be held in contempt of Congress and 
charged with giving false testimony, but when Senator 
Winsgate was arrested and held on corruption charges, 
these calls were withdrawn.</b>

