Then, why don't you go prove yourself?

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.890
Don't sweat it.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.380
I'm a genius, remember?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.400
All right, now we've got all the cards...

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.080
<i>Lupin...</i>

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:18.620
"The man known as Goemon Ishikawa has always 
sought his answers in the heat of battle."

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.860
That's what it says right here.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.430
I'm Yatagarasu with the ICPO.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:42.290
We called ahead. We're here 
to take Fujiko Mine into custody.

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.750
<i>Biometric ID data verified.</i>

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:53.230
<i>The two approved individuals will 
please follow the red pathway.</i>

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.740
Why did you tell Lupin that 
Fujiko Mine had been caught?

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:02.200
To capture his whole gang in one fell swoop.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.660
Sir, you give Lupin too 
much special treatment!

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:10.430
You should just haul him in, like 
you would with any other criminal!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:14.490
If I did that, his gang would
just swoop in and spring him.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:18.830
Even so, his escape wouldn't change 
the fact that you'd actually caught him.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:23.780
Your career has gone nowhere since 
you started working on the Lupin case.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.290
Give it a rest, Yata.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:29.130
No, sir! You deserve better than this!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.340
What the...

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:32.010
Lupin!

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.010
Is that what you wanted?

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.500
That'll do nicely.

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:40.760
Keep all of the elevators except for 
number seven where they are for now.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:54.790
What a coincidence,
 running into you here, Lupin.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:59.670
Well, I figured the biggest business in the 
world might have some <i>crazy</i> loot to steal.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.290
Not seeing much in here, though.

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:05.550
You're doomed, Lupin. Or so I've heard.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.590
You trying to jinx me?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.050
Who told you that?

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:10.540
PeopleLog.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.810
Machines have started 
telling fortunes now?

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:17.660
That's what it came up with after analyzing 
a massive amount of data, apparently.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:21.890
According to PeopleLog, 
"Lupin III has a death wish."

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.140
"He steals jewelry and artworks that 
he only has a passing interest in,

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.990
and the tighter the security, 
the more likely he is to strike."

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.060
Why is that?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.070
I've never been good at riddles.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:37.070
"It's because he has a deep-rooted 
self-destructive impulse."

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.140
And? What if I do?

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.480
Lupin. Steal me.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.830
I'd be a fitting last job 
for Lupin III, wouldn't I?

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.290
"Last job"?

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.160
Why would—

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.000
She doesn't want you to die!

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.370
That's a cute way of interpreting it.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.360
I like how it sounds.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.300
Goemon?

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.370
Looking as surly as ever.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.990
Lupin. I request a duel.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.700
C'mon, man. You seriously want one right now?

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.500
Can't this wait till we're back home?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.510
The nature of our relationship has 
been troubling me for some time now.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:38.510
Words, time, and data 
will never explain it to me.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:41.140
I thought I understood that, but...

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:48.350
Nothing can cut through the clouds 
of doubt the way my Zantetsuken can!

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.370
Answer me, Lupin.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.830
Goemon, this isn't the time to—

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.490
You're on, Goemon.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.800
Lupin?!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.030
This is a personal matter
between him and me.

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:03.360
Time and place don't come into it.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.380
I've got to answer him. 
Right here, right now.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.440
Yata, take the stairs.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.520
Lupin's in the penthouse office.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.510
Yes, Inspector!

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.010
Y'know, Daisuke Jigen...

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:30.190
Partners are a funny thing.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.270
Can it.

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.130
You're not friends.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:35.670
You're like allies, but really, you're rivals.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.720
But none of those are 
accurate descriptions.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.160
There are things you can only 
do with your partner's help.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.880
And some things you have to do...

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.670
...<i>because</i> of your partner.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.010
Can I answer that?

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.760
You know damn well you can't.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.430
It's my partner.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:54.900
I want to introduce you to him.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.160
Yes, this is Ling.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.680
<i>Hey! What're you doing with my partner?</i>

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.950
Are you the boss around here?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.670
Sorry, but we're in the middle of something.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.300
What the hell?!

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:09.130
My name is Ling Bo...

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.450
...and you shouldn't take me lightly.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.060
<i>Tell me, Jigen.</i>

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>Are you really content to spend your life 
as a bit player in the legend of Lupin III?</i>

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.860
Lupin! Goemon! Stop this!

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.190
Calm down.

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:44.690
But...

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.140
If you really love Lupin III, 
you'll keep quiet and watch.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:52.620
No matter what happens, you need 
to be ready to accept the outcome.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:55.450
If you can't, you should set 
your heart on someone else.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.210
<i>Lupin! Are you taking me seriously?</i>

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:07.270
<i>Did you actually intend 
to hit me with that shot?</i>

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.940
<i>Am I just an item in your collection?</i>

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.740
<i>Is that why you hold back when you face me?</i>

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:15.600
<i>Treating me like one of the 
artworks or gemstones you steal...</i>

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:19.720
<i>Like something you choose to sit and 
admire whenever the mood takes you!</i>

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:23.760
<i>Or are you responding to my 
earnestness in a sincere fashion?</i>

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.630
<i>That's it, isn't it?!</i>

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:30.970
Have you forgotten?

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.030
Have you forgotten?!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.560
Nicely done... Goemon...

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.160
Lupin?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.900
Lupin! Lupin?!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.550
Lupin! Say something, Lupin!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.400
Fujiko!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.920
This is the choice he made.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.040
That can't...

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.710
Get out here, Enzo!

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:41.360
You're the one who made 
PeopleLog, aren't you?!

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.920
My name is Ami Enan! I'm your daughter!

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:49.500
Papa... Please save Lupin!

00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:20.890
Lupin, has one of our jobs
 ever gone this far south?

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:24.730
Thanks to PeopleLog, 
you've finally been arrested.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:28.120
In the old days, you would've 
pulled something outta your hat,

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:29.870
and slipped away by now.

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:32.720
This isn't like you, pal.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:35.150
And it's not like you've lost your touch.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:37.910
Maybe guys like you and me are just...

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:41.410
Next time: Just Then, 
An Old Buddy Said Something.

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:44.910
<b>Just Then, An Old Buddy Said Something</b>

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:44.160
Maybe you and I oughta talk 
this over. What do you say?
